rationally the co-ordinates of the <math>n-3</math> fixed points taken upon <math>f</math>, that is, at the least, by taking these to be consecutive points, will involve the co-ordinates of one point of <math>f</math>, and will not be rational in the coefficients of <math>f</math> unless we can specify a point of <math>f</math> whose co-ordinates are rational in these. The curve <math>\text{F}</math> is intersected by a straight line <math>a\xi+b\eta+c=0</math> in as many points as the number of unspecified intersections of <math>f</math> with <math>a\phi+b\phi_1+c\phi_2=0</math>, that is, 3; or <math>\text{F}</math> will be a cubic curve, without double points.

Such a cubic curve has at least one point of inflection <math>\text{Y}</math>, and if a variable line <math>\text{YPQ}</math> be drawn through <math>\text{Y}</math> to cut the curve again in <math>\text{P}</math> and <math>\text{Q}</math>, the locus of a point <math>\text{R}</math> such that <math>\text{YR}</math> is the harmonic mean of <math>\text{YP}</math> and <math>\text{YQ}</math>, is easily proved to be a straight line. Take now a triangle of reference for homogeneous co-ordinates <math>\text{XYZ}</math>, of which this straight line is <math>\text{Y}=0</math>, and the inflexional tangent at <math>\text{Y}</math> is <math>\text{Z}=0</math>; the equation of the cubic curve will then be of the form
{{block center|<math>\text{ZY}^2=a\text{X}^3+b\text{X}^2\text{Z}+c\text{XZ}^2+d\text{Z}^3</math>;}}
by putting <math>\text{X}</math> equal to <math>\lambda\text{X}+\mu\text{Z}</math>, that is, choosing a suitable line through <math>\text{Y}</math> to be <math>\text{X}=0</math>, and choosing <math>\lambda</math> properly, this is reduced to the form
{{block center|<math>\text{ZY}^2=4\text{X}^3-g_2\text{XZ}^2-g_3\text{Z}^3</math>,}}
of which a representation is given, valid for every point, in terms of the elliptic functions <math>\wp(u)</math>, <math>\wp'(u)</math>, by taking <math>\text{X}=\text{Z}\wp(u)</math>, <math>\text{Y}=\text{Z}\wp'(u)</math>. The value of <math>u</math> belonging to any point is definite save for sums of integral multiples of the periods of the elliptic functions, being given by
{{block center|<math>u=\int_{(\infty)}^{(x)}\frac{\text{Z}d\text{X}-\text{X}d\text{Z}}{\text{ZY}}</math>,}}

